      },
      "lineNbr": 53,
      "author": {
        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-04-27T13:56:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do we know if this is a recoverable failure case? Seems pretty bad if we can\u0027t get the mapped ranged from a newly created buffer. Also shouldn\u0027t it be possible for CreateBuffer itself to also fail (e.g. when OOM). Should this whole ctor actually live in an GrDawnBuffer::Make factory where we can return nullptr from in failure cases?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 53,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 53,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "492120f3571caae25c57418686f12d8ef872a8b9",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f05c6c1f_4ed6e066",
        "filename": "src/gpu/ganesh/dawn/GrDawnBuffer.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 53,
      "author": {
        "id": 18529
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-04-27T17:45:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Unfortunately this is not recoverable and there are legitimate situations when this can happen (e.g. if the wgpu::Buffer is invalid because it got created during shutdown, etc). However there is also a bug here that I filed skbug.com/13266 for, which this prevents a crash from.\n\nAs for your suggestion for a factory method: yes, I think that would be better and we\u0027d handle failures at construction gracefully. I can roll that into this CL.",
      "parentUuid": "740f2cf5_fd31a330",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 53,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 53,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "492120f3571caae25c57418686f12d8ef872a8b9",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "484c4c12_ff2e82eb",
        "filename": "src/gpu/ganesh/dawn/GrDawnBuffer.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 70,
      "author": {
        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-04-27T13:56:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "what happens if the buffer is not mappable? blockingMap asserts the buffer is mappable.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 70,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 70,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "492120f3571caae25c57418686f12d8ef872a8b9",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "21386db8_5dcc1157",
        "filename": "src/gpu/ganesh/dawn/GrDawnBuffer.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 70,
      "author": {
        "id": 18529
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-04-27T17:45:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Currently the only way this can get set to true is if the buffer is mappable (see onUnmap below). For non-mappable buffers this should get skipped. It probably makes sense to add an assertion here for this.",
      "parentUuid": "484c4c12_ff2e82eb",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 70,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 70,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "492120f3571caae25c57418686f12d8ef872a8b9",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
